{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "sectional-anatomy",
    "title": "Sectional Anatomy",
    "order": 11
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "breast",
    "title": "Sectional Anatomy: Breast & Chest Wall",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Imaging the Breast and Chest Wall",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Breast planning is done on a CT simulation scan, usually with the arms up on a breast board. The relevant sectional anatomy is the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "chest wall",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " and its muscular/skeletal landmarks, read on soft-tissue window with attention to the lung and heart beneath."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Mid-breast level (intact breast). Identify the breast tissue anteriorly, the pectoralis muscles forming the deep border, the ribs and intercostal spaces, and the lung immediately deep to the chest wall."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The defining geometry is "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "tangential fields",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " skimming the chest wall. How much lung (and, on the left, heart) sits under the tangent on each slice is central to both contouring and verification."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Same Slice on a Lung Window",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Re-windowing the mid-breast slice to a "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "lung window",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " makes the amount of lung under the tangent obvious \u2014 the \"central lung distance\" that predicts pneumonitis risk."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "[Breast soft-tissue window]"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Soft-tissue window",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ": breast, pectoralis, chest wall."
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "[Breast lung window]"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Lung window",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", same level: the lung under the chest wall is now clearly delineated."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "br_p2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Why review the tangential breast field region on a lung window?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "It clearly shows how much underlying lung sits within the tangent, which predicts pneumonitis risk",
              "It improves visualization of the breast skin surface"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A lung window delineates aerated lung crisply, making the central lung distance under the tangent \u2014 a pneumonitis-risk surrogate \u2014 easy to assess."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Muscular and Skeletal Landmarks",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Key structures to identify on the chest wall:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Structure"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Relevance"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Pectoralis major & minor",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Deep border of the breast/chest-wall CTV; pec minor separates axillary node levels"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Ribs / intercostal spaces",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Skeletal reference for chest-wall depth and field borders"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Internal mammary vessels",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Run parasternally \u2014 surrogate for the internal mammary nodal chain"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Humeral head / axilla",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Regional nodal anatomy superolaterally"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Superior level toward the axilla. Identify the pectoralis muscles, the axillary vessels/nodes laterally, and the humeral head."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "br_p3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Which muscle is the landmark separating the axillary lymph node levels?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Latissimus dorsi",
              "Pectoralis minor",
              "Diaphragm"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Pectoralis minor divides axillary levels I (lateral/below), II (behind), and III (medial/above)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Post-Mastectomy Chest Wall",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "After mastectomy the breast mound is gone, and the target becomes the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "chest wall",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " itself \u2014 skin, subcutaneous tissue, and the pectoralis/rib surface. Bolus is often added to bring dose to the skin."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Post-mastectomy chest wall. Note the absent breast tissue, the thin chest-wall target over the pectoralis and ribs, and the immediately adjacent lung."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Compared with an intact breast, the post-mastectomy target is thinner and hugs the lung more closely \u2014 a demanding geometry for sparing lung while covering skin."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Regional Nodes, OARs, and Cardiac Sparing",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Comprehensive treatment may include "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "axillary levels I\u2013III",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "supraclavicular",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "internal mammary",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " nodes. OARs to recognize: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "ipsilateral lung",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "heart and LAD",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (left-sided), and the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "contralateral breast",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Cardiac proximity for left-sided treatment is why "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "deep inspiration breath-hold (DIBH)",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " is common: inflating the lung drops the heart away from the chest-wall tangents, visible slice-by-slice as increased heart-to-chest-wall distance."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "br_p5_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "For a left-sided breast treatment, how does DIBH reduce cardiac dose?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Lung inflation increases the distance between the heart and the chest-wall tangents",
              "It shrinks the breast so fields can be smaller"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "On inspiration the inflated lung displaces the heart away from the tangent beams \u2014 measurable as increased heart-to-chest-wall separation, which verification confirms."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Anatomic Verification for Breast/Chest Wall",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Breast verification balances a deformable soft-tissue target against reproducible bony references."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Surface-guided RT (SGRT)",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " monitors the breast contour and breath-hold in real time."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "kV imaging matched to the "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "chest wall, ribs, and sternum",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " confirms the internal position."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "For DIBH, verification confirms a "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "reproducible breath-hold level",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 both surface and lung/heart position must be consistent."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "br_p6_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "What technology is commonly used to monitor the breast surface and breath-hold in real time during treatment?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Surface-guided radiation therapy (SGRT)",
              "Positron emission tomography (PET)"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "SGRT tracks the external surface continuously, ideal for a soft, mobile breast target and for gating breath-hold."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've compared the intact breast and post-mastectomy chest wall on real CT, seen the same slice on soft-tissue and lung windows, identified the pectoral muscles/ribs/internal-mammary landmarks and nodal regions, and connected cardiac proximity to DIBH and SGRT verification."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Cross-reference: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Breast Treatment Planning"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
